I would upgrade the ram to the largest amount it will fit.  Not for
nethack but for life in general.  Will you be using tiles or playing
the ascii version?  Either way it will run fine but if you are going
to load it in X then pick a lite window manager instead of Gnome or
KDE.  Fluxbox might be you best option with only 2GB of space on the
system.  

> It doesn't say what Linux it comes with but I think I could figure out
> how to compile Nethack on it if it comes with enough tools. 

I haven't compiled it in a while because but if you read the README
file in the tar then you should be good to go.  If you have a network
connection via wifi or cellular service then I wouldn't even bother
compiling it.  Just telnet nethack.alt.org and play over the
internet.  It will save you some disk space.

